            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="da">Cantate som til begge deres kongelige Majestæters Kong Christian den Syvendes og Dronning Caroline Mathildes Salvings-Fest blev opført</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_b21d3ead">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_21">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="_23">Johannes Ewald</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="_22">King Christian VII</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="persName_b811999d">Queen Caroline Mathilde</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_24_0">
               <date isodate="1767" xml:id="date_03616b91">1767</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_24_0">Copenhagen,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_24_0">
               <p xml:id="idm163">After the obligatory year of mourning following the death of <persName xml:id="idm164" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Frederik V</persName> in early 1766, <persName xml:id="idm165" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Christian VII</persName> was now able to hold the ceremony of anointing as the new monarch. The festivities were extensive, and very detailed reports were issued in the newspapers following the event. After the ceremonies in the church, the court and royal couple continued to the palace where the official dinner took place. Scheibe was asked to compose the present cantata for the royal banquet, and for the text the young poet <persName xml:id="idm166" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johannes Ewald</persName>, with whom Scheibe had collaborated on other projects (cf. SchW B2:413, B2:414), was chosen. Part of the text was reprinted in the newspaper, <rend xml:id="idm167" fontstyle="italic">Adresse-Contoirs Efterretninger, </rend>and a text booklet was issued for the event. The music has not survived.</p>
            </history>
